+/*
+ * riscos-mesa: the depth tests below with NEON, eight fragments at a time,
+ * the same bit for bit: a fragment passes when its mask byte is set and
+ * the comparison holds; a failing one gets mask byte 0, a passing one
+ * keeps its mask byte, and (with depth writes on) only passing fragments
+ * write their Z: zfrag cut to 16 bits for a 16-bit buffer, or ORed with
+ * the buffer's top 8 bits for Z24_X8. The comparisons are unsigned 32-bit
+ * ones on the same values the C code compares. Returns how many
+ * fragments it did (a multiple of eight; the C loop does the rest) and
+ * adds the passes to *passed.
